# Cluster : a group of servers. Manager and worker servers.

# Docker swarm is also an orchestration tool similar to k8s. it also has replication feature which helps us to run the required number of replicas in multiple servers.

# Manager: we can have multiple manager servers
-> add or delete workers
-> services: create, delete, update and rollback

# worker:
-> run containers

# Create multiple servers. connect to all of the servers and change their hostnames.

| hostnamectl set-hostname "manager" |

| hostnamectl set-hostname "worker-1" |

| hostnamectl set-hostname "worker-2" |

# install docker in every server

| docker swarm init | creates a swarm with the current server as manager |

[root@manager ~]# docker swarm init
